### Technical Specification: Standardized Filtering & Status Presentation

This update refines the **Account Management** workspace by strictly enforcing a tripartite financial status model and streamlining the filtering interface for immediate, reactive feedback.

#### 1. Updated Filter Behavior Rules
*   **Reactive Filtering**: Results in the table update instantaneously as the user types in the "Client Name" or "Location" fields, or changes the "Payment Status" selection.
*   **Manual Reset Removal**: The dedicated "Reset" button has been removed. Users clear filters by deleting text in inputs or resetting the status dropdown to "All Statuses".
*   **Multi-Criteria Support**: All active filters are applied cumulatively (AND logic).
*   **Simplified Layout**: The filter bar now uses a balanced 3-column grid to maximize the width of search inputs.

#### 2. Status List Cleanup Logic
The system-wide status logic is now bound strictly to the numerical `balance` value of a client's payment record, eliminating the "Unknown" state:

| Balance Condition | Standardized Label | Badge Style |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `balance === 0` | **Fully Paid** | Success (Green) |
| `balance > 0` | **Owing** | Danger (Red) |
| `balance < 0` | **Overpaid** | Purple |

*Any client record failing to provide a valid balance defaults to "Owing" for safety, but the label "Unknown" is purged from all UI components.*

#### 3. UI State Handling (Pseudocode)
```typescript
// State Management
const [filterName, setFilterName] = useState('');
const [filterLoc, setFilterLoc] = useState('');
const [filterStatus, setFilterStatus] = useState('All');

// Filtering Engine (Auto-triggered by state change)
const filteredResults = useMemo(() => {
    return data.filter(item => {
        const statusMatch = filterStatus === 'All' || 
                           calculateStatus(item.balance) === filterStatus;
        const nameMatch = item.name.toLowerCase().includes(filterName.toLowerCase());
        const locMatch = item.location.toLowerCase().includes(filterLoc.toLowerCase());

        return statusMatch && nameMatch && locMatch;
    });
}, [filterName, filterLoc, filterStatus, data]);
```

